Remove the manual deploy: one site, one way to publish it
*"Please remove the manual build. We don't wanna get confused about that. The
documentation about it and everything is just litter."*

`.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare.yml` is deleted, along with the section of
`docs/deploying.md` that existed to explain it.

## What was actually removed

Cloudflare's git build was always the live path. The workflow was a
`workflow_dispatch`-only fallback that built here and pushed `_site` up with
`wrangler deploy`. Between its 99-line header and a page of `deploying.md`, it
was a large share of everything written down about deploying this site — for a
path nobody used.

## I trimmed my own first attempt

The first version of this replaced a 30-line section with a 30-line section
explaining what had been deleted and why, which is the litter you asked me to
remove wearing a different hat. The replacement is now eight lines: there is one
deploy path; here are the three secrets nothing reads any more; the one lesson
worth keeping lives in `TENANCY.md`, where the factory design is what needs it.

## Credentials worth a look while you are in the dashboard

Nothing in this repository now reads any of these:

- `CLOUDFLARE_PAGES_TOKEN` — organization **secret**
- `CLOUDFLARE_PAGES_PROJECT` — repository variable
- `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` — secret or variable

The org secret can be deleted once you are satisfied no other repository in
FC-Public-Media wants it, which I cannot check from here. **The broker is
unaffected** — it uses `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, a differently-named secret.

An unused deploy credential with org-wide scope is exactly the `credentials`
seat's subject, so it is named here rather than left to be rediscovered.

## The one lesson kept, and where

That workflow was manual-only because an earlier version ran on `push` and was
kept harmless *only by the token being absent* — so adding an organization
secret, an ordinary unrelated act, would have started publishing the same site
twice. **Safety that depends on a credential not existing is a landmine with a
note on it.**

That belongs to the factory rather than to a deleted file, and `TENANCY.md`
already carries it. Its two references to the workflow are rewritten to say the
workflow is gone and the hazard returns with the factory.

## Verified

- No reference to `deploy-cloudflare` remains anywhere in `.github/` or `docs/`
  except the one line naming it as deleted.
- The `_config.yml`-cannot-move passage counted "four places" and named it as
  one; now three.
- `python3 site/bin/test_no_secrets.py` — 12 tests, OK (2 skipped).
- Nothing under `site/` changed, and the live deploy path is untouched: this
  removes an alternative, not the thing that publishes.

